// CreateAvatarSessionWithBody Render an avatar into your own LiveKit room (API-key authenticated)
//
// Starts an **avatar session**: the avatar is rendered into a LiveKit room
// that YOU own, on behalf of YOUR agent — the bring-your-own-agent path the
// `livekit-plugins-atmee` plugin uses. Nothing here creates a room or a
// conversation: you mint a LiveKit access token for the avatar participant
// with your own project's API secret (grant `roomJoin` for your room, set the
// participant attribute `lk.publish_on_behalf` to your agent's identity, and
// `kind: agent`) and pass it here. The rendering worker joins your room with
// that token, waits for your agent, receives its audio over the LiveKit data
// stream (`lk.audio_stream`, 16 kHz PCM — livekit-agents'
// `DataStreamAudioOutput`) and publishes synced video and audio.
//
// Responds `202` as soon as the worker acknowledged the start (`status:
// initializing`), typically within a second; the avatar's tracks appear in
// your room a few seconds later. Pass `?waitFor=avatar_joined` to block
// until the worker is in the room instead. Billing runs by the minute while
// the render lasts and stops when the worker reports the end (your agent
// left, the room closed, you removed the avatar participant), when you call
// `POST /v1/avatar_sessions/{id}/end`, or at `maxDurationSeconds`.
//
// The token is read, not verified — your secret never leaves you. A token
// your LiveKit server rejects simply never joins and the session fails as
// `AVATAR_DID_NOT_JOIN` after the join timeout.
//
// **Atmee-hosted room** (no LiveKit project of your own, e.g. a Pipecat
// bot on any transport): omit both `livekitUrl` and `livekitToken`. The
// service then creates a room on Atmee's LiveKit project, the avatar joins
// it as `atmee-avatar-agent` publishing on behalf of `agentIdentity`
// (default `agent`), and the response carries `livekitUrl` and
// `agentToken` for your agent to join that room with. The protocol inside
// the room is the same: stream your agent's audio to the avatar
// (`lk.audio_stream`), subscribe to the avatar's video and audio tracks.
// The room is deleted when the session ends. Requires the `sessions`
// scope; the avatar must be on the key's allow-list.
//
// **v2 avatars** (invite-only) render on a separate GPU pool: the avatar's
// own configuration decides, there is nothing to set on the request. That
// pool scales to zero, so the first v2 session after a quiet period can
// take a few minutes to start: the service waits up to 4 minutes for the
// pool to start the render and up to 6 for the avatar to join. Use
// `?waitFor=avatar_joined` with a client timeout of at least 7 minutes, or
// retry on `avatar_warming`.
